.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md-31-| Apple target integration | The static/source graph builds for the macOS harness and packet-tunnel extension with extension-safe public APIs. iOS delivery remains deferred by ADR-024, not by this SSH decision. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md:32:| Candidate-neutral injection | Core imports no engine types. TCP readiness/I/O, host policy, credential provider, clock, cancellation, logger, observer, metrics, identity generation, and experiment recording remain injected and fakeable. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md:33:| Host key before authentication | Exact raw wire key, negotiated host-key algorithm, and canonical SHA-256 fingerprint reach the host policy before credential lookup or any authentication request. Unknown, changed, algorithm-rejected, and policy-rejected hosts fail closed before auth. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md:34:| Approved public-key authentication | Noninteractive Ed25519 plus an approved deployed fallback work through opaque external signing. Password prompts, agent forwarding, and silent algorithm downgrade are not fallbacks. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md-35-| Approved algorithm policy | KEX, host-key, cipher, MAC, and user-key algorithms are caller constrained; forbidden SHA-1/CBC choices never appear as a compatibility workaround. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md-36-| `direct-tcpip` | Destination and originator are transmitted verbatim; concurrent channels have independent bounded reads, partial writes, EOF, cancel, reset, and close. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md-37-| Exec and stdin upload | One accepted exec request exposes bounded stdin/stdout/stderr and long-lived framing. Relay upload uses exec/stdin only, drains output concurrently, and never invokes SFTP. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md-38-| Client-initiated rekey | Byte-threshold, time-threshold, test, and manual triggers use the production KEX path under active traffic. Rekey failure/timeout stays connection-fatal. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md-39-| Server-initiated rekey handling | Inbound server KEX remains protocol-correct under active traffic without loss, duplication, reordering, or unbounded buffering. Exact reason/lifecycle/generation reporting is the M3 semantic below. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md-40-| Bounded buffers and backpressure | Caller-owned read buffers, queued writes, write-call size, pending operations, callback bridges, and teardown queues have hard positive bounds. A missing exact receive-credit semantic does not permit unbounded buffering. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md:41:| Deterministic cancellation | Resolution, connect, KEX, host decision, credential lookup, auth, open, read, write, EOF, exec, upload, rekey, keepalive, and close waits keep the reviewed operation/channel/connection cleanup scopes. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md-42-| Bounded lifecycle | One serialized owner closes channels, timers, engine session, and socket exactly once; reconnect/network-loss cycles restore owned resources to baseline within injected deadlines. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md:43:| Keychain-only secrets | Configuration and the SSH seam carry opaque credential references and public signing material only. Private keys and passphrases remain in the approved Keychain-backed credential provider and never cross this boundary as configuration bytes. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md:44:| Privacy-safe errors and diagnostics | Typed errors preserve code, phase, scope, retry, and teardown without engine prose or host, user, endpoint, fingerprint, credential, command, path, stream, or payload data. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md-45-| Connection keepalive | The adapter sends the configured SSH keepalive on bounded monotonic scheduling and applies its available failure signal. Exact reply correlation and derived RTT/miss telemetry are the M3 semantic below. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md-46-| Available observability | Connection/channel state, mandatory operation counts, bounded-buffer gauges, protected/payload byte counts, client-rekey triggers/results, keepalive sends, and any cheaply available facts remain typed and privacy-safe. Unavailable deep facts use explicit deferred states. |
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md-47-
