.temp/resources/TASK-260728-7ii1xz/TASK-260728-7ii1xz_macos-credential-transport-decision.md-261-| secret lifetime / zeroization | secret is at rest in root context indefinitely. Best-effort clearing only (see common ground). Weaker than B by design; that is the price of unattended start |
.temp/resources/TASK-260728-7ii1xz/TASK-260728-7ii1xz_macos-credential-transport-decision.md-262-| blast radius | provider compromise ⇒ the SSH private key. Root compromise ⇒ the same, since `SystemKey` is root-readable — the System keychain is **not** protected by the user's login password. Item *attributes* are world-readable (E5: 192 items dumped as uid 502), so attributes must carry no hostname, account, or profile name. Item *data* is ACL-gated (E7 blocked on an authorization prompt) |
.temp/resources/TASK-260728-7ii1xz/TASK-260728-7ii1xz_macos-credential-transport-decision.md-263-| entitlement / portal cost | **zero.** `application.sb:792-793` grants `/Library/Keychains` read+write to any process holding `com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension`; `application.sb:655-656` grants the `securityd`/`SecurityServer` Mach lookups to every sandboxed process. No `keychain-access-groups`, no temporary exception, no new portal capability, no new App ID, no C1 change |
.temp/resources/TASK-260728-7ii1xz/TASK-260728-7ii1xz_macos-credential-transport-decision.md:264:| testability | best. The `SecItem` file-based path is exercisable in unit tests against a throwaway keychain file under `.temp/` via `kSecUseKeychain`, giving `TASK-260715-379cpk` / `TASK-260715-1o9wjz` a real test seam without a signed sysex; the root-context leg is one focused check inside `TASK-260715-9yp8to` |
.temp/resources/TASK-260728-7ii1xz/TASK-260728-7ii1xz_macos-credential-transport-decision.md-265-| **cannot guarantee** | (a) that the user's login password protects the secret — it does not; (b) synchronous revocation **in every provider state**. It *is* available whenever the NE configuration is installed and enabled, because an app-originated message launches a non-running provider (§5.0); it is **not** available when the configuration is disabled, unapproved, or removed, or when no host is running (§5.2); (c) that the `SecItem`→file-based shim exposes everything needed — TN3137 warns *"when you use it to target the file-based keychain it operates through a shim. That shim has limitations"*, so the restrictive `SecAccess` must be verified, not assumed; (d) the root-context write itself is not locally proven (§3.3) |
